 produces $(Y)$ and $(Z)$. Both $(Y)$ and $(Z)$ give lodoform test positive. Only $(Y)$ gives Tollen's test positive.\nChoose the correct statements.","explanation":"$\\begin{aligned} & \\mathrm{C}_4 \\mathrm{H}_8 \\mathrm{O} \\\\ & \\text { D.U. }=4+1-4=1\\end{aligned}$\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/modules/ms/ja/eM-8iQBSwDwY76caq_ggFI4x32OdpCc2M-ve-YZcqgw.original.fullsize.png\"/><br/>"},{"id":310508,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Alcohols Phenols and Ethers","exam":"Engineering","examName":"Most Important Selected Qs for JEE Advanced","q":"Which of the following pairs can be distinguished by using Lucas Test?","options":["$\\mathrm{PhCH}_2 \\mathrm{OH}, \\mathrm{CH}_3 \\mathrm{CH}_2 \\mathrm{OH}$","$\\mathrm{PhCH}_2 \\mathrm{OH}, \\mathrm{PhOH}$","\\left(\\mathrm{CH}_3\\right)_2 \\mathrm{CHOH}, \\mathrm{CH}_3 \\mathrm{CH}_2 \\mathrm{CH}_2 \\mathrm{OH}","$\\mathrm{CH}_3 \\mathrm{CH}_2 \\mathrm{CH}_2 \\mathrm{OH}, \\mathrm{CH}_3 \\mathrm{CH}_2 \\mathrm{OH}$"],"answer":2,"solution":"(A)\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\mathrm{Ph}-\\mathrm{CH}_2-\\mathrm{OH} \\xrightarrow[\\text { conc. } \\mathrm{HCl}]{\\text { anh. } \\mathrm{nCl} \\mathrm{Cl}_2} \\mathrm{Ph}-\\mathrm{CH}_2-\\mathrm{Cl}+\\mathrm{Zn}(\\mathrm{OH}) \\mathrm{Cl} \\text { (immediate) } \\\\\n& \\text { (white turbidity) } \\\\\n& \\mathrm{CH}_3-\\mathrm{CH}_2-\\mathrm{OH} \\xrightarrow{\\text { Lucas reagent }} \\mathrm{CH}_3-\\mathrm{CH}_2-\\mathrm{Cl}+\\mathrm{Zn}(\\mathrm{OH}) \\mathrm{Cl}\n\\end{aligned}$\n(B) $\\mathrm{Ph}-\\mathrm{CH}_2-\\mathrm{OH} \\xrightarrow[\\text { reagent }]{\\text { Lucas }} \\mathrm{PhCH}_2 \\mathrm{Cl}+\\mathrm{Zn}(\\mathrm{OH}) \\mathrm{Cl}$ (immediate)\n(White turbidity)\n$\\mathrm{Ph}-\\mathrm{OH} \\xrightarrow[\\text { reagent }]{\\text { Lucas }} \\text { No reaction under normal condition }$\n(C)\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\left(\\mathrm{CH}_3\\right)_2 \\mathrm{CH}-\\mathrm{OH} \\xrightarrow[\\text { reagent }]{\\text { Lucas }}\\left(\\mathrm{CH}_3\\r